      "worked": "Each distinct object is a bin; its count records how many times it is selected. Thus an unordered selection corresponds to distributing $n$ identical stars among $r$ distinct bins, allowing empty bins.\n\nSeparate the bins with $r-1$ identical bars. There are $n+r-1$ positions altogether, and choosing the positions of the bars determines the selection.\n\n$$N=\\binom{n+r-1}{r-1}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
